From: Iscle <albertiscle9@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: skip RRO startup when disabled

mt7996_register_device() calls mt7996_dma_rro_start() even when hardware
receive reordering is disabled. In that case its queues have not been
allocated, but startup still registers and enables their NAPI instances.
The descriptor-based teardown loop skips these zero-length queues,
leaving enabled NAPI instances behind when the dummy netdev is freed.

Return before registering RRO NAPI or enabling RRO interrupts if the
device has no active hardware receive reordering mode. This matches the
condition used when allocating the RRO queues.

On an MT7992 with RRO disabled, this prevents four NAPI deletion warnings
and leaves no registered receive NAPI instances after DMA cleanup.

---
--- a/mt7996/dma.c
+++ b/mt7996/dma.c
@@ -624,6 +624,9 @@ void mt7996_dma_rro_start(struct mt7996_de
 {
 	u32 irq_mask;
 
+	if (!mt7996_has_hwrro(dev))
+		return;
+
 	if (mtk_wed_device_active(&dev->mt76.mmio.wed)) {
 		irq_mask = dev->mt76.mmio.irqmask |
 			   MT_INT_TX_DONE_BAND2;
